NCERT's sketch of the evolution of plant forms through geological periods places them in this order:
- **Zosterophyllum** is among the earliest vascular land plants, at the base of the sketch;
- **ferns** (pteridophytes) came next;
- the seed plants (gymnosperms) followed, with **Ginkgo** an ancient gymnosperm line;
- the **Gnetales** arose later, beside the line that leads to the flowering plants.

So the order is (iii), (i), (ii), (iv), and the answer is option (B) (iii), (i), (ii), (iv).
